spec ww04-update-rollback-then-delete-explicit: 2 sessions, 6 permutations
# WW04, rollback arm (update rolls back), explicit second writer. s1 updates n and
# ROLLS BACK; the vacuum is drained immediately after (H1); s2, open since before
# s1's write, deletes n and commits. Only interleavings with the drain adjacent to
# the rollback run.
# The second writer is an EXPLICIT transaction that BEGINs before
# either session's first step, so its snapshot predates the ROLLBACK. A ROLLBACK
# aborts its transaction (rmp #2973): once it is drained, the older snapshot's write
# must succeed, exactly as the autocommit arm's does. Before #2973 the ROLLBACK
# published a commit record and this write was refused.

starting permutation: s1u s1rb s1dr s2d s2c
step s1u: MATCH (n:Item {name:'n'}) SET n.x = 1 RETURN n.x AS x
x
-
1
(1 row)
step s1rb: ROLLBACK
step s1dr: <vacuum drain>
step s2d: MATCH (n:Item {name:'n'}) DETACH DELETE n RETURN count(*) AS deleted
deleted
-------
1      
(1 row)
step s2c: COMMIT
final final: MATCH (n:Item) RETURN n.name AS name, n.x AS x ORDER BY name
name|x
----+-
"m" |0
(1 row)

starting permutation: s1u s2d s1rb s1dr s2c
step s1u: MATCH (n:Item {name:'n'}) SET n.x = 1 RETURN n.x AS x
